N2  - A systematic review of 23 training studies (491 participants, mostly men) concluded that resistance-trained people need rests longer than 2 minutes to maximise strength gains. For untrained people, 60-120 s is enough, and rests under 60 s still produce solid gains.
N1  - Systematic review (PRISMA, 5 databases, no pooled meta-analysis seen) of chronic training studies comparing rest interval durations; 23 studies, 491 participants (413 males, 78 females); studies rated good-to-moderate methodological quality. Grgic, Schoenfeld, Skrepnik, Davies, Mikulic. Sports Med 2018;48(1):137-151.. Verified 2026-10-14. Used for: training.inter_set_rest: supports
