DO  - 10.1007/s11332-025-01605-5
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1007/s11332-025-01605-5
N2  - In 17 untrained men doing knee extensions for 10 weeks, one leg rested 20 s and did extra sets to match the volume of the other leg, which rested 2 minutes. Thigh muscle growth did not differ (rectus femoris +14.3% vs +16.7%), and neither did strength gain (1RM +42.4% vs +41.5%).
N1  - Within-subject training study: 17 untrained young men (mean age 25.3), each leg doing a different condition. LONG: 10RM, 3-4 sets to failure, 2-min rest. SHORT: 10RM, sets to failure until reps matched LONG, 20-s rest. Unilateral knee extension, 2x/week for 10 weeks. Randomisation of legs not confirmed. Attarieh et al., Sport Sci Health 2026;22: article 32. A Correction notice exists (doi:10.1007/s11332-026-01758-x).. Not verified 2026-10-14. Used for: training.inter_set_rest: context
