N2  - In 28 young people training knee extensions at 80% 1RM for 10 weeks, 3-minute rests gave more quadriceps growth than 1-minute rests with the same sets (13.1% vs 6.8%). However, 1-minute rests with extra volume matched it (12.9%), and 3-minute rests held to the lower volume grew less (6.6%). Strength rose similarly in all groups.
N1  - Within-subject training study: 28 subjects, each leg allocated to 1 of 4 unilateral knee-extension protocols at 80% 1RM, 2x/week for 10 weeks. LI: 3-min rest. SI: 1-min rest. VLI-SI: 1-min rest with volume load matched to LI. VSI-LI: 3-min rest with volume load matched to SI. Random allocation not confirmed in the text I saw. Longo et al., J Strength Cond Res 2022;36(6):1554-1559 (epub 2020).. Not verified 2026-10-14. Used for: training.inter_set_rest: context
